[Music]  for the first time in recent history the  u.s. arrested a Chinese intelligence  officer this week and brought him to  America to face charges  eunjin Xu is accused of stealing  intellectual property and trade secrets  from u.s. aviation and aerospace  companies a report from the US Trade  Representative says China's economic  espionage costs the u.s. between 225 and  600 billion dollars a year john carlin  helped bring the first-ever charges  against Chinese hackers he co-authored a  new book called dawn of the code war  carlins served as assistant attorney  general for national security in the  Obama administration welcome John  morning ok put this this arrest in  perspective here of young Jin Xiu the  look it's one of the first times ever if  not the first time that you've been able  to catch one of the puppet masters from  overseas in China who's running  intelligence operatives inside the  United States day in day out and  stealing secrets so for an American this  would be like if one of our CIA agents  got busted in some other country and was  brought to trial is that the equivalent  essentially and they cleverly got him to  leave China they almost never leave  China into a third country where he'd be  subject to arrest and it shows that this  new strategy it's not just bringing  charges to name and shame and layout the  theft that's happening of American  intellectual property it's that their  real charges and that people face real  consequences including jail cells give  us a sense of so there's intellectual  property theft  there's meddling and elections give us a  sense of the whole smorgasbord of  threats here yeah one of the reasons I  wrote the book is that there are so many  instances that people think are science  fiction that have already happened  including terrorists stealing from  retail companies personally identifiable  information of customers in order to  have plots to kill them including  Chinese espionage that's driven  companies into bankruptcy costing real  jobs inside America and most troubling  is that the next time we get into a  military conflict are very fighter jets  with our research and development that  spent years in the  making could be used against us to kill  our servicemen and when it comes to  cyber warfare a lot of focus has been on  Russia and rightly so but FBI director  Christopher Rea just this week said  Russia is fighting today's fight China  is fighting tomorrow's fight the next  day and the day after it's you right  that's one of the things so you think  about our economy and our military and  even our electrical grid the electricity  that we have before us it is all  dependent now on digital technology we  moved almost everything we value from  books and paper to digital over a  25-year period and we did so while  discounting risk China in particular  along with Russia North Korea and Iran  recognized that vulnerability and  they're hitting us day in day out we are  in a code war now and to direct a raise  point what we're seeing is when it comes  to next-generation technology artificial  intelligence the way all of our phones  connect wirelessly that China is getting  the lead and they're doing it not by  playing fair not by investing in  research and development but by stealing  it and using our own technological  know-how against us are we doing enough  to combat it No  so I think and partly it's because it's  reason I wrote the book is that people  don't realize today how vulnerable we  are when I go out to talk to businesses  they're surprised by the inside story of  cases that we've already brought and  these are all cases that we successfully  figured out who did it we're much better  that than people think the problem is  after we bring these cases after you  call out China after you call out Russia  for not Pecha which caused billions of  dollars of damage to companies around  the world  there's no follow-on consequence that  forces them to change behavior so it  sounds like we're not winning the code  war and I just want to quote from a new  government report that found almost all  of the u.s. military's newly developed  weapon systems have quote  mission-critical  cyber vulnerabilities so why has the  government so far failed to protect our  defense systems well partly we need to I  think for a long time we thought there  was a technical fix where you know you  do it right and you're safe and that  doesn't exist the technology that we're  basing this on the internet itself uses  a protocol that was never designed with  security  in mind we can do better and we need to  right now to your point is is that  devices our cars the peacemakers in our  hearts are now using that same  technology we can't make the same  mistake that allowed our Social Security  numbers to get stolen to cause actual  life-and-death consequences and there  are actions that we can take we should  be looking at our phones and some of our  devices a bit differently thank you so  much for talking about this very  important subject Thank You hate it and  Donna the code Wars goes on sale October  16th

